    "type": "question",
    "label": "10",
    "prompt": "The formula for the surface area $S$ cm² of a rectangular prism is $S=2(\\ell w+\\ell h+hw)$, where $\\ell$, $w$ and $h$ are the length, width and height of the prism, measured in cm. If $S=80$, $\\ell=5$ and $w=2$, find $h$, the height of the prism.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$4\\frac{2}{7}$ cm",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}80&=2(5\\times2+5h+2h)\\\\80&=20+10h+4h\\\\60&=10h+4h\\\\60&=14h\\\\\\frac{30}{7}&=h\\\\h&=4\\frac{2}{7}\\end{align*}$$\nThe height of the rectangular prism is $4\\frac{2}{7}$ cm.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
